generatedCommentsNodes.comment:
`getLocalAddress()` does not guard against `getLocalInetAddress()` returning `null`. The `getLocalInetAddress()` method catches all exceptions and falls through to `return null`. Calling `normalizeHostAddress(null)` will then throw a `NullPointerException` at `localHost.getHostAddress()` (since `null instanceof Inet6Address` is `false`). The old code had this call inside a `try-catch`, so the NPE was swallowed; the new code does not.
Suggested fix:
```java
public static String getLocalAddress() {
    InetAddress localHost = getLocalInetAddress();
    if (localHost == null) {
        return null;
    }
    return normalizeHostAddress(localHost);
}
```

